    "suggested_action": "The most important improvement is to generate matched, same-cell-state functional datasets for the exact cells used in HepG4-seq and HBD-seq: perform biological replicates of Pol II CUT&Tag or ChIP-seq and ChIP-seq or CUT&Tag for H3K4me3, H3K27ac, H3K36me3, H3K4me1, and H3K27me3, plus RNA-seq and ATAC-seq in HEK293 and mESCs, rather than relying on external histone or RNA-seq resources such as GSE86189. This directly addresses the gap in [(Zyner et al., 2022-01)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d62d57b98bdcab61e2fff24835345c58e9da1894) and [(Shen et al., 2021-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/970cc41034350f60328e48aa6ecab90c6cf895fd) and makes the proposed correlation between co-localized G4/R-loop peaks and regulatory architecture testable. The next most important action is to compare four genomic categories with statistical rigor: co-localized G4/R-loop peaks, G4-only peaks, R-loop-only peaks, and matched background or negative-control regions, using peak counts, fold enrichment, Mann-Whitney tests, q-values, IDR for replicate concordance, and GO enrichment, as the plan already specifies. Because [(Shen et al., 2021-05)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/970cc41034350f60328e48aa6ecab90c6cf895fd) shows promoter G4 formation can occur without active transcription, the plan should separate Pol II occupancy from transcriptional output by using Pol II ChIP or CUT&Tag together with RNA-seq and, if feasible, nascent RNA assays or H3K36me3 as an independent mark of productive elongation, while using ATAC-seq or MNase-seq to account for chromatin compaction. The plan should also add R-loop-specific validation controls, including RNase-treated HBD-seq, RNase H1 hybrid-binding domain specificity controls, and a subset comparison with S9.6 ChIP or CUT&Tag or another orthogonal R-loop assay, to ensure that the functional enrichment is not driven by HBD background or by G4-only loci. Finally, the functional characterization should be integrated with the helicase-regulation arm by comparing co-localized peak annotation and gene activity in wild-type versus Dhx9 knockout mESCs and after ML216 or NSC617145 treatment, overlaying Dhx9 CUT&Tag peaks, and reporting all reproducibility-critical details: cell lines, passage, biological replicate number, sequencing platform and read depth, hemin/biotin aniline concentrations, EGFP-V5-HBD expression level, Tn5 or CUT&Tag parameters, peak-caller and thresholds, DESeq2 parameters, and statistical significance for each enrichment and differential-expression test.",
